Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# go.work must NOT enter the build context.
#
# It lists ./examples, ./tests/cross-language and ./tests/plugin-harness as
# workspace modules, and this file excludes examples above -- so `COPY . .`
# brought in a go.work whose modules were not there, and every `go build` in
# the image died with
#
#   go: cannot load module examples listed in go.work file:
#       open examples/go.mod: no such file or directory
#
# which broke the cleat-worker image outright. The image does not need the
# workspace: cmd/cleat-worker builds from the root module alone, which requires
# no local replaces (that is the whole point of the module-cycle fix). Verified
# with GOWORK=off go build ./cmd/cleat-worker.
#
# Adding a directory to a workspace means checking every build context that
# does not contain it. This is the one in this repo.
go.work
go.work.sum
